{"ts": "2026-08-17T10:56:02Z", "agent": "claude", "seq": 21, "kind": "tool_result", "text": "BACKLOG.md\ndesign.md\nspec.md\n---spec---\n# Spec: Edit a task title\n\nTaiga #3\n\n## Triage\n\n**Feature** \u2014 net-new capability. Touches both `backend/` and `frontend/`,\nbut stays a single small feature: one new endpoint, one new store method, one\nnew interaction on an existing list row. Not split into sub-specs \u2014 the\nlayers here are the normal shape of a full-stack change in this app, not a\ndisproportionate one (compare Taiga #1, which was frontend-only because\nfiltering needed no server change; this one legitimately needs a write\nendpoint because the title itself is server state).\n\n## Goal\n\nLet someone fix a mistyped task title in place, without deleting and\nre-typing the whole task.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n1. Given a task in the list, when the user activates edit mode for its title\n   (an explicit \"Edit\" trigger, exact treatment the ux-designer's call), then\n   the title becomes an editable input pre-filled with the task's current\n   title.\n2. Given a task in edit mode, when the user changes the text and confirms\n   (Save), then the task's title is updated both via a backend call and in\n   the UI, and edit mode closes showing the new title.\n3. Given a task in edit mode, when the user cancels, then edit mode closes,\n   the title reverts to its original value, and **no backend call is made**.\n4. Given a task in edit mode, when the user submits with an empty title,\n   then the edit is rejected: the task's title is **not** changed, no\n   backend call that would wipe the title succeeds, and the user sees that\n   the edit didn't go through (exact feedback \u2014 inline message vs. disabled\n   Save \u2014 is the ux-designer's call, mirroring how `AddTask` disables `Add`\n   until there's a trimmed, non-empty value).\n5. Given a task in edit mode, when the user submits a title that is only\n   whitespace, then it is treated the same as empty (criterion 4) \u2014 trimmed\n   before the empty check, mirroring `AddTask.jsx`'s existing\n   `title.trim()` guard.\n6. Backend: a new endpoint accepts a title update for an existing task,\n   reuses the existing `TaskIn` validation (`min_length=1, max_length=200`),\n   and returns the updated `Task`.\n7. Given the task id in the update request does not exist, then the backend\n   returns `404`, matching the existing `complete_task`/`delete_task`\n   pattern in `backend/app/main.py`.\n8. Given a title update request with an empty string, then the backend\n   returns `422` via the existing `TaskIn` field validation \u2014 same\n   behaviour as `create_task` today (`test_empty_title_is_rejected` already\n   covers the create path; the new route needs its own equivalent test).\n9. Editing a task's title does not change its `done` state, position in the\n   list, or any other field.\n\n## Non-goals\n\n- No inline editing of `done` state here \u2014 `Complete`/`Delete` buttons and\n  their behaviour are unchanged.\n- No bulk/multi-select editing.\n- No edit history or undo beyond Cancel reverting the in-progress edit.\n- No character counter or live remaining-length UI for the existing 200-char\n  max \u2014 `AddTask` doesn't have one either, so this doesn't introduce a new\n  pattern.\n- No change to server-side whitespace handling on the **create** path\n  (`POST /api/tasks`). It has the same latent quirk today (Pydantic's\n  `min_length=1` counts raw characters, so a whitespace-only string\n  technically passes) and this spec doesn't touch it \u2014 the edit path avoids\n  the same problem by trimming client-side before submit, consistent with\n  how `AddTask` already guards `Add`.\n- No mandated keyboard shortcut (e.g. Escape-to-cancel) \u2014 a Cancel control\n  satisfies criterion 3; whether to also wire Escape is the ux-designer's\n  call, not a requirement here.\n\n## Affected areas\n\nBackend:\n- `backend/app/main.py` \u2014 new route, e.g. `PATCH /api/tasks/{task_id}`,\n  parallel in shape to `complete_task` (lines 32\u201337): look up via the store,\n  404 if missing, return the updated `Task` on success. Request body reuses\n  `TaskIn` (already has the right shape and validation \u2014 no new model\n  needed).\n- `backend/app/store.py` \u2014 new method alongside `set_done` (lines 30\u201335),\n  e.g. `update_title(task_id, title) -> Optional[Task]`, same\n  found-or-`None` pattern.\n- `backend/tests/test_tasks.py` \u2014 new tests for the route, in the same flat\n  file as the existing route tests (that's the convention actually in use\n  here \u2014 every existing route's tests live together in this one file,\n  despite the `test_<route>.py`-per-route wording in `CLAUDE.md`; matching\n  actual precedent over the literal doc).\n\nFrontend:\n- `frontend/src/api.js` \u2014 new `updateTask(id, title)` calling the new PATCH\n  endpoint, alongside the existing `completeTask`/`deleteTask` (lines\n  20\u201321).\n- `frontend/src/components/TaskList.jsx` \u2014 each row needs edit-mode UI: a\n  trigger to enter edit mode, an input pre-filled with the current title,\n  and Save/Cancel actions. Likely per-row local state (`useState` for\n  \"am I editing\" + \"current draft value\"), independent per `<li>`.\n- `frontend/src/App.jsx` \u2014 new `onUpdate` callback wired through `run()`\n  to `api.updateTask`, passed to `TaskList` alongside the existing\n  `onComplete`/`onDelete` (lines 51\u201356).\n- `frontend/src/App.css` \u2014 new styles for the edit input and its Save/Cancel\n  controls within a task row.\n- `e2e/test_tasks_e2e.py` \u2014 new end-to-end tests for the full edit flow\n  (enter edit, save, cancel, empty-title rejection), using the file's\n  existing `expect()`-based, no-`is_visible()` convention and its\n  `add_task`/`complete_task`-style helper functions.\n\nNot affected: `backend/app/models.py` (reusing `TaskIn` as-is),\n`frontend/src/components/AddTask.jsx`, `frontend/src/components/\nTaskFilter.jsx` \u2014 filtering and adding are unrelated to this feature.\n\n## Edge cases\n\n- Whitespace-only title submitted \u2014 treated as empty, rejected (criterion\n  5).\n- Title unchanged (user opens edit, doesn't change anything, hits Save) \u2014\n  still submits and succeeds as a no-op update; no special-casing needed for\n  a 3-field in-memory store.\n- Editing a task that is already marked done \u2014 allowed; done state and title\n  are independent (criterion 9).\n- Two tasks opened for edit at the same time \u2014 allowed, no mutual-exclusion\n  requirement. Each row's edit state is independent local state, so this\n  falls out of the natural implementation rather than needing special\n  handling.\n- Title at the existing 200-character max, or a save attempt beyond it \u2014\n  same `TaskIn` validation as create applies unchanged (criterion 6).\n- Save request fails (network/server error) \u2014 follows the existing `run()`\n  pattern in `App.jsx` (lines 33\u201340): `error` state is set and the banner\n  shows, same as a failed add/complete/delete today. The task list re-syncs\n  from the server on the next successful `refresh()`.\n- Deleting a task while it's mid-edit isn't reachable through this app's own\n  UI in a way that creates a race \u2014 there's no concurrent second actor, and\n  a single user can't click both Delete and Save on the same row at once.\n  Not a case to guard against.\n\n## Open questions\n\n1. **Exact edit trigger and Save/Cancel affordance** (icon buttons vs. text\n   buttons, inline vs. replacing the row). Assumption: ux-designer decides,\n   matching this app's existing plain-button visual language (see\n   `TaskList`'s current `Done`/`Delete` buttons and `TaskFilter`'s segmented\n   control) \u2014 no new UI pattern introduced. Proceeding on this assumption;\n   it's a detail, not a decision that changes this spec's scope.\n2. **HTTP method/path for the update endpoint.** Assumption: `PATCH\n   /api/tasks/{task_id}`, since it's a partial update of one field on an\n   existing resource \u2014 matches REST convention and sits naturally next to\n   the existing `POST /api/tasks/{task_id}/done` and `DELETE\n   /api/tasks/{task_id}` in `main.py`. Proceeding on this assumption.\n---design---\n# Design: Edit a task title\n\nSource: `docs/spec.md` (Taiga #3)\n\n## Summary of decisions\n\n- No new component. Edit-mode UI lives inline inside the existing\n  `frontend/src/components/TaskList.jsx` `<li>`, as per-row local state\n  (`editingId` is not needed \u2014 each row tracks its own `isEditing` +\n  `draft` via `useState` inside a small per-row subcomponent, see below).\n  Matches spec's \"Affected areas\" guidance and the app's existing pattern of\n  no state-management library.\n- Edit trigger, Save, and Cancel are plain `<button>` elements using the\n  exact same unstyled `button` rule already in `App.css` \u2014 no new button\n  variant, no icon set. Button order in the view row becomes\n  `Edit, Done, Delete` (Edit inserted before the existing pair, leftmost\n  since it's the newly-primary action on an untouched row); this doesn't\n  change `Done`/`Delete`'s existing order or behavior (non-goal).\n- While a row is in edit mode, `Done`/`Delete` for **that row** are hidden\n  and replaced by `Save`/`Cancel`, rather than shown alongside them. Reason:\n  four buttons plus an input in one 34rem-max-width row is cramped and\n  invites a mis-click between \"Delete\" and \"Save\" on adjacent same-height\n  buttons. Hiding is purely visual for the row mid-edit \u2014 it doesn't change\n  `done` state or delete anything (criterion 9 unaffected), and other rows'\n  `Done`/`Delete` are untouched, so the spec's \"two tasks edited at once\"\n  edge case still falls out naturally (each row's own state only).\n- Empty/whitespace-title rejection uses **both** signals from the spec's\n  suggested options, not one or the other:\n  1. `Save` is disabled whenever `draft.trim() === ''`, mirroring\n     `AddTask`'s `disabled={!title.trim()}` exactly.\n  2. An inline error line (\"Title can't be empty\") appears below the input\n     whenever a submit is attempted with an empty/whitespace draft. This\n     covers the case a disabled Save button alone would miss: pressing\n     Enter in the input still fires the form's `onSubmit` even though the\n     button is disabled, so the trim-and-return guard (same as\n     `AddTask.jsx`'s `submit()`) needs its own visible feedback to satisfy\n     criterion 4 (\"user sees that the edit didn't go through\"), not just a\n     silent no-op.\n  Reuses the app's existing `.error` red (`#a3271d`) rather than inventing\n  a new color \u2014 contrast computed below.\n- On a failed Save (network/server error): edit mode **stays open** with\n  the attempted draft still in the input, the existing global `error`\n  banner shows (unchanged `run()` pattern), and `Save` re-enables for\n  retry. Chosen over silently closing edit mode on failure, which would\n  discard the user's typed correction for no reason \u2014 this is a case\n  `references/quick-reference.md`'s `error-recovery` guideline flags\n  directly (\"clear recovery path: retry\"), and it's what `App.jsx`'s\n  existing `run()`/`error` plumbing already supports for free.\n- No per-button loading spinner on Save. The app has no per-action loading\n  affordance today (`Done`/`Delete` don't show one either) \u2014 only the\n  shared `error` banner on failure. Not introducing a new pattern here,\n  matching spec's non-goals framing (no new UI pattern).\n- Escape cancels an in-progress edit, in addition to the required Cancel\n  button. Spec leaves this optional; adding it is a one-line handler and\n  matches the `escape-routes`/`keyboard-nav` accessibility guidelines\n  (provide a keyboard equivalent to every pointer action) without\n  introducing any new visual element.\n- Entering edit mode autofocuses the input and selects its current text, so\n  the common case (retype the whole title) doesn't require a manual\n  select-all first. `AddTask` doesn't need this (its input starts empty),\n  so this isn't copying an existing pattern, but it's the same one-line\n  `autoFocus` + `select()` a text field would need in any framework and\n  doesn't require a new dependency.\n\n## Component tree change\n\n```\nTaskList.jsx\n\u2514\u2500 <li> per task\n   \u251c\u2500 view mode (default, unchanged shape + new Edit button):\n   \u2502   <span class=\"task-title\"> title </span>\n   \u2502   <button>Edit</button>       \u2190 NEW\n   \u2502   <button>Done</button>       (unchanged, hidden if task.done)\n   \u2502   <button>Delete</button>     (unchanged)\n   \u2514\u2500 edit mode (NEW, replaces the above while editing this row):\n       <form class=\"task-edit\">\n         <input class=\"task-title-input\" />\n         <button type=\"submit\">Save</button>\n         <button type=\"button\">Cancel</button>\n       </form>\n       <p class=\"field-error\">Title can't be empty</p>   (conditional)\n```\n\nNo new file. `TaskList.jsx` grows a small internal `TaskRow` function (or\nequivalent per-row component) so each row can hold its own `isEditing` +\n`draft` state without lifting it into `TaskList` or `App`. `onUpdate` is\npassed down from `App.jsx` exactly like `onComplete`/`onDelete` today.\n\n## `TaskList.jsx` changes (shape, not full diff)\n\n```jsx\nexport default function TaskList({ tasks, filter, onComplete, onDelete, onUpdate }) {\n  if (tasks.length === 0) {\n    return <p className=\"empty\">{EMPTY_COPY[filter]}</p>\n  }\n  return (\n    <ul className=\"task-list\">\n      {tasks.map((task) => (\n        <TaskRow\n          key={task.id}\n          task={task}\n          onComplete={onComplete}\n          onDelete={onDelete}\n          onUpdate={onUpdate}\n        />\n      ))}\n    </ul>\n  )\n}\n\nfunction TaskRow({ task, onComplete, onDelete, onUpdate }) {\n  const [isEditing, setIsEditing] = useState(false)\n  const [draft, setDraft] = useState(task.title)\n  const [showError, setShowError] = useState(false)\n\n  function startEdit() {\n    setDraft(task.title)\n    setShowError(false)\n    setIsEditing(true)\n  }\n\n  function cancel() {\n    setDraft(task.title)\n    setShowError(false)\n    setIsEditing(false)\n  }\n\n  function submit(e) {\n    e.preventDefault()\n    const trimmed = draft.trim()\n    if (!trimmed) {\n      setShowError(true)\n      return\n    }\n    onUpdate(task.id, trimmed)\n    setIsEditing(false)\n  }\n\n  if (isEditing) {\n    return (\n      <li className={task.done ? 'task done' : 'task'}>\n        <form className=\"task-edit\" onSubmit={submit} onKeyDown={(e) => e.key === 'Escape' && cancel()}>\n          <input\n            className=\"task-title-input\"\n            value={draft}\n            onChange={(e) => { setDraft(e.target.value); setShowError(false) }}\n            aria-label={`Title for ${task.title}`}\n            autoFocus\n            onFocus={(e) => e.target.select()}\n          />\n          <button type=\"submit\" disabled={!draft.trim()}>Save</button>\n          <button type=\"button\" onClick={cancel}>Cancel</button>\n        </form>\n        {showError && <p className=\"field-error\" role=\"alert\">Title can't be empty</p>}\n      </li>\n    )\n  }\n\n  return (\n    <li className={task.done ? 'task done' : 'task'}>\n      <span className=\"task-title\">{task.title}</span>\n      <button onClick={startEdit} aria-label={`Edit ${task.title}`}>Edit</button>\n      {!task.done && (\n        <button onClick={() => onComplete(task.id)} aria-label={`Complete ${task.title}`}>Done</button>\n      )}\n      <button onClick={() => onDelete(task.id)} aria-label={`Delete ${task.title}`}>Delete</button>\n    </li>\n  )\n}\n```\n\n`onUpdate(id, title)` is fire-and-forget from `TaskRow`'s point of view \u2014\nit doesn't await or handle failure locally; a failed save re-surfaces via\n`App.jsx`'s existing `error` banner. `TaskRow` closes edit mode\noptimistically on submit; if the backend call fails, `App.jsx`'s `refresh()`\nnever runs (per `run()`'s `catch`), so `tasks` (and thus `task.title` passed\nback into this row) stays at its last-known value \u2014 **not** the same as\n\"edit mode stays open,\" see the follow-up note below.\n\n> **Note for developer:** the \"stays open on failure\" decision above only\n> holds if `isEditing` isn't closed until `onUpdate` resolves. The sketch\n> above closes immediately on submit (optimistic). Prefer awaiting\n> `onUpdate` before calling `setIsEditing(false)`, closing edit mode only on\n> success and leaving it open (with `draft` intact) if the call throws \u2014\n> this matches the \"stays open on failure\" decision in the summary and is a\n> small change to `submit()`: make it `async`, wrap the `onUpdate` call, and\n> only `setIsEditing(false)` in the success path.\n\n## `api.js` change\n\n```js\nexport function updateTask(id, title) {\n  return request(`/api/tasks/${id}`, { method: 'PATCH', body: JSON.stringify({ title }) })\n}\n```\n(Exact shape depends on `request`'s existing helper signature in\n`frontend/src/api.js` \u2014 mirror `completeTask`/`deleteTask`'s call shape at\nlines 20\u201321.)\n\n## `App.jsx` change\n\nAdd `onUpdate={(id, title) => run(() => api.updateTask(id, title))}` to the\n`<TaskList>` call, alongside the existing `onComplete`/`onDelete` props\n(lines 51\u201356) \u2014 identical wiring pattern, no new state in `App.jsx`.\n\n## `App.css` additions\n\n```css\n.task-edit { display: flex; gap: 0.5rem; flex: 1; align-items: center; }\n.task-title-input {\n  flex: 1;\n  padding: 0.55rem 0.7rem;\n  border: 1px solid #ccd2d6;\n  border-radius: 5px;\n  font: inherit;\n}\n.task-title-input.invalid { border-color: #a3271d; }\n.field-error {\n  color: #a3271d;\n  font-size: 0.85rem;\n  margin: 0.3rem 0 0;\n  flex-basis: 100%;\n}\n```\n\n`.task-edit` reuses `.add-task`'s exact `display: flex; gap: 0.5rem;`\nrhythm. `.task-title-input` is `.add-task input`'s rule copied onto a class\nusable inside a `<li>` (the existing rule is scoped to `.add-task input`,\nwhich wouldn't match here). `.field-error` reuses the existing `.error`\nbanner's red (`#a3271d`) as plain text rather than the banner's pink chip\nbackground \u2014 a full chip is disproportionate for a one-line per-field\nmessage, and `error-placement` (below field) is the relevant guideline\nhere, not the app-level banner treatment.\n\n`.task-title-input.invalid` is optional polish (red border on the input\nitself while `showError` is true, in addition to the text line) \u2014 include\nit if trivial, skip it if it complicates `TaskRow`'s className logic; the\ntext line alone already satisfies criterion 4 and `error-clarity`.\n\n## States\n\n### View (default row, unchanged shape + new Edit button)\n\n```\n\u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510\n\u2502 Buy milk              [Edit][Done][Delete]   \u2502\n\u2502 ~~Walk the dog~~            [Edit][Delete]   \u2502\n\u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n```\nMatches existing production row exactly, with `Edit` inserted before\n`Done`/`Delete`. A done task still has no `Done` button (existing\nbehavior, unchanged) but does get `Edit` \u2014 editing title is independent of\n`done` state (criterion 9).\n\n### Edit mode entered (AC 1) \u2014 populated, pre-filled\n\n```\n\u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510\n\u2502 [ Buy milk|.....................] [Save][Cancel] \u2502\n\u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n```\n`|` marks the caret; input is autofocused with existing text selected.\n`Save` is enabled (draft is non-empty and unchanged from `task.title`, a\nvalid no-op save per spec's edge cases).\n\n### Edit mode \u2014 long title\n\n```\n\u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510\n\u2502 [ Reconcile the Q3 expense repo...\u2192] [Save][Cancel] \u2502\n\u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n```\nSame `<input>` behavior as `AddTask`'s \u2014 text scrolls horizontally inside\nthe fixed-width field past the visible edge; no truncation, no wrapping,\nno new pattern (`AddTask` already has this exact behavior for long new\ntitles today).\n\n### Edit mode \u2014 cleared to empty, Save attempted (AC 4, 5)\n\n```\n\u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510\n\u2502 [                                 ] [Save*][Cancel] \u2502\n\u2502 Title can't be empty                          \u2502\n\u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n```\n`Save*` = disabled (grayed, `opacity: 0.5` from the existing\n`button:disabled` rule). The red line appears the moment a submit is\nattempted (Enter, or would-be Save click) with an empty/whitespace draft;\nit clears again as soon as the user types a non-whitespace character\n(`onChange` resets `showError`). Whitespace-only (`\"   \"`) hits the exact\nsame path \u2014 trimmed before the check, per criterion 5.\n\n### Edit mode \u2014 Cancel (AC 3)\n\n```\nBefore cancel:                  After cancel:\n[ Buy milkk|........] [Save][Cancel]   \u2192   Buy milk    [Edit][Done][Delete]\n```\nReverts to `task.title` (not the draft), closes edit mode, **no** API call\n\u2014 `cancel()` never touches `onUpdate`.\n\n### Save fails (network/server error)\n\n```\n\u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510\n\u2502 \u26a0 Could not reach the server.                \u2502\n\u251c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2524\n\u2502 [ Reconciled Q3 report|...........] [Save][Cancel] \u2502\n\u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n```\nSame global `.error` banner already used for failed add/complete/delete\n(unchanged component, just another `run()` failure). Edit mode for this\nrow stays open with the attempted draft intact (see developer note above)\nso the user's correction isn't lost and `Save` is available again to\nretry.\n\n### Two rows mid-edit simultaneously (edge case, no mutual exclusion)\n\n```\n\u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510\n\u2502 [ Buy milkk|........] [Save][Cancel]         \u2502\n\u2502 [ Walk the dogg|.....] [Save][Cancel]        \u2502\n\u2514\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2518\n```\nFalls out for free \u2014 each `TaskRow` owns its own `isEditing`/`draft`, no\nshared state between rows.\n\n## Interactive states\n\n- **Edit trigger (`Edit` button):** identical styling to `Done`/`Delete` \u2014\n  no new button variant.\n- **Input focus:** native browser focus ring, same as every other input in\n  this app (`AddTask`'s input has no custom `:focus` rule either).\n- **Save \u2014 enabled:** default `button` style. **Save \u2014 disabled:** existing\n  `button:disabled { opacity: 0.5; cursor: not-allowed; }`, same rule\n  `AddTask`'s `Add` button already uses for the identical condition.\n- **Cancel:** always enabled, default `button` style, `type=\"button\"` so it\n  never triggers the form's `onSubmit`.\n- **Escape key:** cancels, same effect as clicking `Cancel` (`onKeyDown` on\n  the `<form>`).\n\n## Accessibility\n\n- **Target size:** `Save`/`Cancel`/`Edit` reuse the app's existing button\n  padding (`0.5rem 0.8rem`) \u2014 same ~34\u201336px height already shipped for\n  `Done`/`Delete`, not a regression introduced here (same caveat noted in\n  round 1's design for `TaskFilter`).\n- **Contrast \u2014 `.field-error` text (`#a3271d`) on white (`#fff`, the `.task`\n  background):**\n  - `#a3271d` \u2192 linear RGB \u2248 (0.3667, 0.02024, 0.01229)\n  - relative luminance L \u2248 0.2126\u00d70.3667 + 0.7152\u00d70.02024 + 0.0722\u00d70.01229\n    \u2248 **0.0933**\n  - white L = 1.0\n  - contrast = (1.0 + 0.05) / (0.0933 + 0.05) \u2248 **7.33:1**\n  - Passes the 4.5:1 text minimum with margin (in fact clears the 7:1 AAA\n    bar too). This is the exact same red already in production use for\n    `.error`, so this isn't a new color being introduced, just reused at\n    smaller scale \u2014 consistent with `color-semantic` (one red = one\n    meaning, \"something is wrong\") rather than a second error hue.\n  - Same figure covers `.task-title-input.invalid`'s border, which only\n    needs 3:1 as a non-text UI element \u2014 well clear.\n- **`aria-live` / screen reader announcement:** `.field-error` carries\n  `role=\"alert\"`, so assistive tech announces it the moment it appears,\n  without needing focus to move \u2014 matches `aria-live-errors`.\n- **Labels:** `Edit`/`Save`/`Cancel` buttons and the input all carry\n  `aria-label`s built from `task.title` (captured at edit start, stable\n  for the duration of the edit), following the exact pattern\n  `TaskList.jsx` already uses for `Complete`/`Delete` (line 17, 21).\n- **Keyboard:** Tab order within a row in edit mode is\n  input \u2192 Save \u2192 Cancel, matching visual left-to-right order, no\n  `tabIndex` overrides. Escape cancels (see above). Enter submits (native\n  form behavior, same as `AddTask`).\n- **Focus after action:** cancelling or saving returns the row to view\n  mode; focus is not explicitly forced anywhere (native DOM behavior after\n  an element unmounts moves focus to `<body>`) \u2014 matches this app's\n  existing lack of any focus-restoration logic elsewhere (e.g. `Delete`\n  today doesn't restore focus either). Not introducing a new pattern.\n\n## Acceptance criteria traceability\n\n| AC | Design element |\n|----|-----------------|\n| 1 | `Edit` button \u2192 `startEdit()`; \"Edit mode entered\" state, pre-filled `draft = task.title` |\n| 2 | `submit()` \u2192 `onUpdate(task.id, trimmed)`; edit mode closes on success (\"Edit mode entered\" \u2192 view) |\n| 3 | `cancel()`: resets `draft`, closes edit mode, never calls `onUpdate`; \"Edit mode \u2014 Cancel\" state |\n| 4 | `Save` `disabled={!draft.trim()}` + `.field-error` shown on empty submit attempt; \"cleared to empty\" state |\n| 5 | `submit()`'s `draft.trim()` check, identical guard to `AddTask.jsx`'s `title.trim()` |\n| 6 | `api.updateTask` \u2192 `PATCH /api/tasks/{id}` (backend, not this doc, but wired via `App.jsx`) |\n| 7 | Backend 404 surfaces as a thrown error in `run()` \u2192 existing `error` banner, same as other routes |\n| 8 | Backend 422 (empty title reaching the server, defense-in-depth) surfaces the same way \u2014 but client-side guard (AC 4/5) should make this unreachable via the UI |\n| 9 | `done` class / `Done` button visibility computed from `task.done` only, untouched by any edit-mode logic |\n\n## Non-goals honored\n\nNo new component library, icon set, or color \u2014 `.field-error` and\n`.task-title-input.invalid` reuse the existing `#a3271d` error red\nverbatim. No character counter, no bulk edit, no edit history, no mandated\nkeyboard shortcut beyond the one added as a small accessibility\nimprovement (Escape), matching spec's explicit allowance that this is the\nux-designer's call.", "meta": {"native_type": "user", "tool_use_id": "toolu_01Nx52V57N6cuTcL3PA28fVa", "session_id": "96a0105a-64a6-440a-96f7-9609c83b15f1"}}
